          "guid": "mt3z863bcmfajk0x",
          "message": {
            "text": "For static controls, alpha is the discriminator between source-frame RGB and isolation ownership. A composited source PNG cannot reveal foreground RGB at partially transparent checkbox/radio edges, so source RGB is copied only when Chromium's isolated surface proves alpha 255; all other pixels retain isolated RGBA. Time-dependent owners deliberately bypass this merge and take the atomic source crop. See also src/render/element-tree-to-svg.ts.",
            "markdown": "For static controls, alpha is the discriminator between source-frame RGB and isolation ownership. A composited source PNG cannot reveal foreground RGB at partially transparent checkbox/radio edges, so source RGB is copied only when Chromium's isolated surface proves alpha 255; all other pixels retain isolated RGBA. Time-dependent owners deliberately bypass this merge and take the atomic source crop. See also src/render/element-tree-to-svg.ts."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/native-control-raster.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 168,
                  "endLine": 190,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/**\n * Merge a same-coordinate source crop with the isolated alpha surface.\n * Source RGB is safe only for pixels whose isolated alpha is 255: no backdrop\n * can contribute there.  Partially transparent pixels retain Chromium's\n * isolated premultiplied result and alpha exactly.\n */\nexport function composeNativeControlFrames(\n  isolated: Uint8Array,\n  source: Uint8Array | null,\n  sourceOccluded: boolean,\n): Uint8Array | null {\n  if (isolated.length === 0 || isolated.length % 4 !== 0) return null;\n  if (source != null && source.length !== isolated.length) return null;\n  const result = new Uint8Array(isolated);\n  if (source == null || sourceOccluded) return result;\n  for (let offset = 0; offset < result.length; offset += 4) {\n    if (isolated[offset + 3] !== 255 || source[offset + 3] !== 255) continue;\n    result[offset] = source[offset];\n    result[offset + 1] = source[offset + 1];\n    result[offset + 2] = source[offset + 2];\n  }\n  return result;\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
