          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt3zpagc9qjbpcnh",
          "message": {
            "text": "Time-dependent native paint must use one atomic source crop, not RGB from one frame plus alpha from a later isolation frame. The zero-tolerance browser oracle exposed premultiplication and moving-edge drift at that seam. An overlap-free source crop is safe because the same structural backdrop is emitted underneath; an intersecting painted owner instead forces the named fail-closed route.",
            "markdown": "Time-dependent native paint must use one atomic source crop, not RGB from one frame plus alpha from a later isolation frame. The zero-tolerance browser oracle exposed premultiplication and moving-edge drift at that seam. An overlap-free source crop is safe because the same structural backdrop is emitted underneath; an intersecting painted owner instead forces the named fail-closed route."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/native-control-raster.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 488,
                  "endLine": 506,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      if (target.raster.frameSensitive === true) {\n        if (source == null || sourceCrop == null || fact.sourceOccluded) {\n          pushRequiredRasterWarning(options.warnings, target, \"time-dependent paint could not retain one overlap-free source frame\");\n          continue;\n        }\n        // Alpha from the isolation screenshot belongs to a later compositor\n        // frame. Even a byte-exact RGB merge would move antialiased pixels on\n        // an indeterminate progress segment. With no intersecting owner, the\n        // complete source crop is the only coherent atomic stamp; its backdrop\n        // is already the same paint the structural renderer emits underneath.\n        const png = await sharp(Buffer.from(source), {\n          raw: { width: sourceCrop.width, height: sourceCrop.height, channels: 4 },\n        }).png().toBuffer();\n        target.raster.dataUri = `data:image/png;base64,${png.toString(\"base64\")}`;\n        target.raster.x = plan.output.x;\n        target.raster.y = plan.output.y;\n        target.raster.width = plan.output.width;\n        target.raster.height = plan.output.height;\n        continue;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
